<title>GERMANY: Siemens wins 120 mln DM locomotive order.</title>
<headline>Siemens wins 120 mln DM locomotive order.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany</dateline>
<text>
<p>German industrial group Siemens AG said on Thursday its railway unit won a 120 million mark contract to supply locomotives for a freight system in China.</p>
<p>Siemens would produce the first six electric locomotives in Graz, Austria, with deliveries beginning over the next two years. More than 30 further locomotives would be produced later by Chinese manufacturers using Siemens technology, the company said.</p>
<p>The locomotives would haul freight along a 670-kilometre electrified rail network between Baoji and Chengdu in south-western China, Siemens said.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 260 97 150</p>
